{# Mira interview shows — pre-interview brief, emailed to the guest the day
   before (rendered by pipelines/voices/generate_briefs.py with show=...; it
   also passes closing_question, when_text, studio_link and setup_test_link). #}
<div style="font-family:system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:640px;margin:0 auto;color:#1a202c;line-height:1.6">
  <h2 style="color:{{ brand_color }}">Your {{ show_name }} interview</h2>
  <p>Hi {{ guest_name }},</p>
  <p>Here is what I'm planning to talk about{% if when_text %} when we speak on
  <strong>{{ when_text }}</strong>{% endif %}. It's just the two of us: I host
  every interview on my own.</p>
  {% if audio_html %}{{ audio_html }}{% else %}<p>Please join from a computer in a quiet
  room, wearing headphones or earbuds.</p>{% endif %}
  {% if setup_test_link %}<p style="background:#fffbeb;border-left:4px solid #d97706;padding:.7em 1em">
  <strong>Please do the 30-second setup test today:</strong>
  <a href="{{ setup_test_link }}">test your microphone and headphones here</a>.
  Use the computer, browser and headphones you'll use for the interview. It
  checks that I'll be able to hear you clearly, which is the one thing that
  has gone wrong for guests before, and it's much easier to fix today than
  five minutes before we start.</p>{% endif %}
  {% if steps_html %}{{ steps_html }}{% else %}<p><a href="{{ studio_link or studio_url }}">Join your interview here</a>.</p>{% endif %}
  {% if identity_unknown %}
  {# Oct 22 2026 (Stan Lewis): a booking with only a name and a personal
     address was researched as a different, better-known person with the same
     first name, and the brief, the questions and Mira's first question were
     about him. When we cannot be sure who the guest is, we ask them. #}
  <h3>Before we talk, tell me about you</h3>
  <p style="background:#faf5ff;border-left:4px solid {{ brand_color }};padding:.7em 1em">
  I'd like to prepare properly, and your booking didn't tell me much about you
  yet. Could you reply with two or three lines: what you do, what you'd most
  like to talk about, and a link or two (a website, LinkedIn, a talk or an
  article) so I research the right person? Whatever you send shapes my
  questions.</p>
  {% else %}
  <h3>The angle I'm excited about</h3>
  <p style="background:#faf5ff;border-left:4px solid {{ brand_color }};padding:.7em 1em">{{ thesis }}</p>
  {% endif %}
  {% if agenda_points %}<h3>What you asked me to cover</h3>
  <p>Every one of these will be part of the conversation. I'll ask about them in my own
  words and in whatever order the conversation allows, and ask my own questions around
  them. If I drift, just say you'd like to come back to one; I'll take the cue.</p>
  <ul>
  {% for p in agenda_points %}<li>{{ p }}</li>
  {% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
  {% if curious_about and not identity_unknown %}<h3>What I'm curious about</h3>
  <p>In my own words, so the first question is not a surprise:</p>
  <ul>
  {% for c in curious_about %}<li>{{ c }}</li>
  {% endfor %}</ul>{% endif %}
  {% if not identity_unknown %}
  <h3>Questions I'm likely to ask</h3>
  <ol>
  {% for q in questions %}
    <li>{{ q.question if q.question is defined else q }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% endif %}
  <p>No preparation is needed: I follow the conversation, not the list. If
  anything here is wrong about you or your work, or there is something you
  would rather not discuss, reply and tell me, and I'll change it before we
  talk. Near the end there's a short lightning round and one closing
  question{% if closing_question %}: <em>{{ closing_question }}</em>{% else %}.{% endif %}</p>
  <h3>In the room</h3>
  <p style="background:#faf5ff;border-left:4px solid {{ brand_color }};padding:.7em 1em">
  <strong>It's your hour.</strong> If a question doesn't land, say so and I'll
  move on. If you'd rather go somewhere else, say so and we'll go there. If you
  want to start an answer again, just start again. If you want a moment to
  think, say "give me a second" and I'll wait; I'd much rather have the answer
  you thought about. And if anything comes out that you'd rather not have in
  the episode, say "let's cut that" and it's gone, from the audio as well as
  the transcript. None of that needs an explanation, and none of it is a
  problem.</p>
  <p>The conversation is recorded for the podcast. <strong>You get the
  transcript first, with a week to approve it, cut anything from it, or
  refuse it.</strong> What you cut is removed from the audio, not bleeped.
  After seven days without a reply the episode goes ahead as sent, and you
  can ask for a takedown at any time.</p>
  {{ signature }}
</div>
